BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Peter Hutton: Two Rivers + In Titan's Goblet
DTSTART:20251205T033000Z
DTEND:20251205T044500Z
DTSTAMP:20251205T033000Z
UID:gEw34OvuK0
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 57 mins (0h57m)\n\nPresented by Mount Analogue ○ 
 Art + Cinema Two films by Peter Hutton\, described as “one of cinema’s
  most ardent and poetic portraitists of city and landscape\,” projected 
 in their original 16mm format. Two Rivers (2003\, 47 min.) presents contem
 plative\, observational portraits of the Hudson and the Yangtze rivers. In
  Titan’s Goblet (1991\, 10 min)\, takes its title from the Hudson River 
 landscape painting by Thomas Cole\, and inscribes ever-so-subtle patterns 
 and movements of sky\, sun\, moon\, and fire.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cine
 ma/in-theaters/peter-hutton-two-rivers-in-titans-goblet\n\nEstimated start
 : 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
